"""Professional QuickBooks-to-Infinium sales reconciliation.

Run with:
    python -m streamlit run app.py

The app produces two files from one controlled reconciliation run:
    1. Sales_Reconciliation_<run>.xlsx
       Raw Data, Reconciled Data, Unresolved Exceptions, and
       Product Aggregate Summary.
    2. Sales_Reconciliation_Analytics_<run>.xlsx
       Optional technical evidence, normalization, method analytics,
       controls, and run configuration.

Standard QuickBooks and Infinium column names are populated automatically on
upload. A guided ingestion flow leads users through both files, mapping review,
reconciliation, and final review while retaining optional mapping overrides.
Harmless blank columns and repeated in-file header rows are removed with an
import audit, while malformed sources and implausible mappings are blocked
before reconciliation. Strict match passes use vectorized one-to-one joins.

Design principle: uncertain matches are never guessed. Automatic matches must
be unique, one-to-one, and exact at the signed-cent level. Grouped and
variance-based matches are prohibited.
"""

